{"runs":[[0,17,0,"Every onTaskDispatched export is discovered with its taskQueueTrigger and registered as a queue; a caller can register queues directly with the official defaults, an invalid queue id and an over-limit concurrency are rejected."],[17,11,0,"Enqueue over the wire: a named task and an auto-named task reach the default-config handler with the X-CloudTasks headers; duplicate names, unknown queues and caller headers overriding the emulator's are recorded."],[28,5,0,"Retry semantics: a 500 keeps the execution count, a 400 increments it, exhausting maxAttempts runs maxAttempts+1 times, and the previous response reaches the handler."],[33,6,0,"A dispatch deadline aborts the emulator's request while the handler completes (a retry follows); maxConcurrentDispatches 1 serialises a queue; maxDispatchesPerSecond 1 paces one."],[39,9,0,"Deleting a pending task, an unknown task, a task on an unknown queue, and a task already dispatched; the Admin SDK's delete swallows 404."],[48,11,0,"The Admin SDK path handlers use: getFunctions().taskQueue().enqueue() with data, id, scheduleDelaySeconds, dispatchDeadlineSeconds, headers and uri, a duplicate id, an unknown queue, an explicit region; delete() of a pending, an unknown and an auto-named task."],[59,1,0,"The Admin SDK path handlers use: getFunctions().taskQueue().enqueue() with data, id, scheduleDelaySeconds, dispatchDeadlineSeconds, headers and uri, a duplicate id, an unknown queue, an explicit region; delete() of a pending, an unknown and an auto-named task."]],"cases":[{"t":"backends","q":"GET /backends","a":"200 {backends}","r":"c","k":"answer"},{"t":"startup logs","q":"emulator log lines matching \"queue\"","a":"0 log lines matched","r":"c","k":"behaviour"},{"t":"stats initial","q":"GET /queueStats","a":"200 {queue:{project}, queue:{project}, queue:{project}, queue:{project}, …}","r":"c","k":"answer"},{"t":"register defaults","q":"POST /projects/{project}/locations/us-central1/queues/manual-defaults","a":"200 {tas